    "scope": "The retained Q1286541 reference, signed reservoir shoreline, crest-side service road and separate native powerhouse identify Mangla. In the model frame +X points east and +Z south. The selected 3,350.958 m visual ridge trace is distinct from the 3,140 m retained source length. The western ridge follows the lake edge and standard terrain fit, and its downstream gate locations are provisional. The map places the powerhouse on the separate eastern outlet. The native footprint mask replaces only that one mapped hall. All 800 road fragments, including the downstream bridge, are retained.",
    "notes": "The western spillway gate axis is an estimate from photographs and the mapped tail channel. The retained water polygon starts at the runout and does not establish an upstream connection at the authored gate. A narrow gap remains outside the west chute wall, and DEM transitions are visible at the embankment and canal edges. The auxiliary works, exact gate count and operating levels need geographic review. Keep the placement provisional."
  },
